# Next.js 16 (App Router)

## Source of truth

Read bundled docs in `node_modules/next/dist/docs/` before using unfamiliar APIs. Key upgrade traps:

- `middleware` → **`proxy`** (`proxy.ts`, export `proxy`)
- `params` / `searchParams` are **`Promise`s** — `await` them in pages, layouts, route handlers
- App lives under `src/app`; keep using App Router only

## File conventions

| File | Role |
| --- | --- |
| `layout.tsx` | Shared chrome; root layout required |
| `page.tsx` | Route UI (Server Component by default) |
| `loading.tsx` | Instant loading UI / Suspense boundary |
| `error.tsx` | Segment error boundary (Client Component) |
| `not-found.tsx` | 404 UI |
| `route.ts` | Route Handler (HTTP endpoints) |
| `proxy.ts` | Request proxy (rewrites, redirects, headers) |

Private folders: `_components`, `_lib` (not routable). Route groups: `(marketing)` do not affect the URL.

## Composition pattern (preferred)

```tsx
// src/app/page.tsx — Server Component
import { Hero } from "@/components/hero";

export default function Page() {
  return (
    <main>
      <Hero /> {/* client island only if needed */}
    </main>
  );
}
```

- Keep `page.tsx` / `layout.tsx` as Server Components whenever possible.
- Push `"use client"` into leaf components (e.g. animated sections), not the whole page.
- Export `metadata` or `generateMetadata` from Server Components only — never from client files.

## Navigation & assets

- Internal links: `next/link` (not `<a href="/...">`).
- Images: `next/image` with explicit `width`/`height` or `fill` + sized parent.
- Fonts: `next/font/google` or `next/font/local` in the root layout; expose CSS variables for Tailwind.
- Scripts: `next/script` for third parties.

## Data & caching

- Fetch in Server Components close to the data source.
- Do not call Route Handlers from Server Components (extra hop).
- Use Route Handlers for client-triggered HTTP; prefer Server Actions for mutations/forms when added.
- Be intentional with `cookies()`, `headers()`, and `searchParams` — they opt into dynamic rendering.
- Parallelize independent fetches; use `loading.tsx` / Suspense to stream.

## Proxy

- Use `src/proxy.ts` or root `proxy.ts` for header/rewrite/redirect logic.
- Prefer `redirects` / `rewrites` in `next.config.ts` for static cases.
- Proxy is not for slow data fetching or full auth session management.

## Quality bar

- Match patterns in `01-app/02-guides/production-checklist.md`.
- After route or config changes: `npm run build`.
